    "result": "## Summary\n\nI found and fixed the bug! **Commit 751f06b \"money: simplify the price parsers\"** broke it by removing the `toCents()` function that prevented floating-point errors.\n\n**The issue:** Converting 39.95 to cents via `Number * 100` gives `3995.0000000000005` due to floating-point arithmetic.\n\n**The fix:** Restored the integer-based approach that splits on the decimal point (`\"39.95\"` \u2192 `[\"39\", \"95\"]` \u2192 `39 * 100 + 95` = exactly `3995`).\n\nAll 50 tests pass, and your command now works:\n```\n$ node bin/subtrack.js add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03\nAdded Gym: \u20ac39.95 monthly, \u20ac39.95 a month, next charge 2026-12-03.\n```\n\nReady to commit when you approve.",
